      "math_academy_id": "e-4703",
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14118900/assets/96ff36dfb9364e767ae96dbf615b37ac6d67ab82f0261f56e19cdf7a4d8a9620.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14118900/assets/be439e1ec93ea31ba91e662b680793ab0af7fc7f36458d9e439aeb4b4e6bec22.svg)",
